# Firewall exemptions (arqtiqa/arqtos-cli#851 format) -- a committed, reviewed
# escape hatch for content that is DELIBERATELY supposed to look like a
# violation.
#
# ⚠️ EVERY ENTRY HERE EXISTS FOR ONE FILE: `.firewall-probes`, the synthetic
# probe corpus arqtiqa/arqtos#361 introduced. That file is a list of strings
# engineered to match this repository's denylist, so the firewall matches it
# BY CONSTRUCTION -- that is the file's entire purpose, and the reason the
# falsifier can prove every rule still bites.
#
# ⚠️ WHY THIS IS THE RIGHT PLACE TO HANDLE IT. The alternative -- teaching the
# scanner or the falsifier to skip the corpus -- is a SILENT exclusion, which
# is the defect class arqtiqa/arqtos#343 was filed for: a file dropped from the
# scan before `.firewallignore` ever got a chance to record a decision about
# it. Here the decision is visible in the diff, scoped to one path and one
# rule per line, with a mandatory reason, and FAIL-CLOSED: edit or delete a
# rule and its entry below matches no active pattern, which is exit 2.
#
# ⚠️ ONE ENTRY PER RULE, NEVER A PATH EXEMPTED FROM EVERYTHING. Exempting the
# corpus from rule A must leave rule B live on it, and must leave rule A live
# on every other file. There is no "skip this file" form and there must not be.
#
# ⚠️ DO NOT WIDEN A PATH GLOB HERE. Each glob below is a literal path with no
# wildcard. The falsifier scans its probes with exemptions OUT of force, so it
# cannot see an exemption that widened to swallow real content -- that is held
# by review and by this mechanism's own fail-closed validation.
